---
title: CatLium EduTech — Async AI Generation (job lifecycle)
---
%%{init: {'htmlLabels':false,'sequence':{'useMaxWidth':false}}}%%
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant B as Browser (Next.js)
    participant N as nginx
    participant GC as GenerationController<br/>(or QuestionBank…)
    participant G as GenerationService
    participant JS as JobsService
    participant RMQ as RabbitMQ (ai_generation)
    participant W as worker-ai consumer (concurrency 5)
    participant AI as OmniRoute gateway<br/>POST /v1/chat/completions
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    B->>N: POST /content/generate {materialId, operation}
    N->>GC: /api/v1/content/generate
    GC->>G: validate scope (material ACTIVE+READY, dedup key)
    G->>JS: issueJob(type=AI_GENERATE_*)
    JS->>DB: INSERT jobs (status='queued')
    JS->>RMQ: publish(message {jobId, instituteId, type, payload})
    RMQ-->>JS: ack
    JS-->>G: job
    G-->>B: 202 ACCEPTED {jobId}  (async, never blocks)

    loop Every WORKER_AI_CONCURRENCY seconds — client polls
        B->>GC: GET /content/generation-status / jobs/:jobId
        GC->>DB: SELECT job
        DB-->>GC: status
        GC-->>B: {status: queued|processing|completed|failed}
    end

    RMQ->>W: deliver message (prefetch 1)
    W->>DB: UPDATE jobs SET status='processing', startedAt
    W->>DB: resolve source → READY materials (ACTIVE), build context chunks (40k char budget)
    loop Each context chunk (12k chars, 400 overlap)
        W->>AI: POST /chat/completions {model, messages, temperature:0.2}
        AI-->>W: raw JSON response
    end
    W->>W: parse_json_object → Pydantic schema validate (per-type)
    W->>W: aggregate + deterministic dedup (questions by stem, flashcards front/back…)
    W->>DB: persist content_items / questions (AI_GENERATED + provenance, PENDING)
    W->>DB: UPDATE jobs SET status='completed', result, completedAt
    Note over W,DB: Failure: transient responses and transport errors retried with backoff (max 3).<br/>Terminal error → job marked 'failed', never left 'processing'.

    B->>B: render fetched content / question bank